        "raw_bytes": 1473,
        "lf_bytes": 1473,
        "raw_sha256": "2be554d84baf1f2b796ade05fba49271b5d05e4e8d2d46427d47a6756f85c8f9",
        "lf_sha256": "2be554d84baf1f2b796ade05fba49271b5d05e4e8d2d46427d47a6756f85c8f9"
      },
      "byte_range": [
        98826,
        100299
      ],
      "literal_source_text": "X\\sim\\mu\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\ \\text{independently}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY=X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,. (2.7)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2.SS1.p1",
      "coverage": "NODE",
      "reason": "Real joint space/conditional projection context; extension to canonical scalar is ASTIS adapter, not source graph substitution.",
      "qualified_raw_slice": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p1-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
        "raw_bytes": 19341,
        "lf_bytes": 19341,
        "raw_sha256": "395059e86bc44a9581440d09e7095e1979f6579e14a55979f5bd2fa382b6fb24",
        "lf_sha256": "395059e86bc44a9581440d09e7095e1979f6579e14a55979f5bd2fa382b6fb24"
      },
      "qualified_LF_slice": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p1-dffe0a792ef0.LF.snapshot",
        "raw_bytes": 19341,
        "lf_bytes": 19341,
        "raw_sha256": "395059e86bc44a9581440d09e7095e1979f6579e14a55979f5bd2fa382b6fb24",
        "lf_sha256": "395059e86bc44a9581440d09e7095e1979f6579e14a55979f5bd2fa382b6fb24"
      },
      "byte_range": [
        708364,
        727705
      ],
      "literal_source_text": "Our target distribution is the joint law \\pi_{\\eta} defined in ( 2.6 ), and we set \\mathfrak{H}\\coloneqq L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) . Recall from ( 3.11 ) that the ideal Proximal BPS has transition kernel \\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)=\\delta_{2x-y}(\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime})\\,\\bigl[\\rho\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y^{\\prime}}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})+(1-\\rho)\\,\\mathcal{H}_{y^{\\prime}}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})\\bigr]\\,, where \\mathcal{H}_{y^{\\prime}} is the conditional half-turn kernel from Proposition 3.2 . Since the algorithm is a discrete-time chain, its evolution is described by the induced one-step Markov operator on observables, (\\mathsf{K}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{2d}}f(x^{\\prime},y^{\\prime})\\,\\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)\\,. Thus \\mathcal{K} acts on probability laws, whereas \\mathsf{K} is its induced action on observables. The first term in brackets in \\mathcal{K} is the conditional resampling branch. After the auxiliary coordinate is updated to y^{\\prime} , this branch replaces the x -coordinate by an independent draw from \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y^{\\prime}} . The associated conditional expectation operator is (\\mathsf{P}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int f(x^{\\prime},y)\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})=\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y=y]\\,. (B.1) In particular, \\mathsf{P}f depends only on the coordinate y . The range and kernel of \\mathsf{P} are \\begin{split}\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:f(x,y)=g(y)\\text{ for some }g\\in L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})\\}\\,,\\\\ \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\ker(\\mathsf{P})=\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y]=0\\}\\,.\\end{split} (B.2) Here \\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\coloneqq I-\\mathsf{P} , so \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} and f=\\mathsf{P}f+\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}f . In the common terminology of hypocoercivity [ 14 , 21 ] , \\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}) is the macroscopic subspace and its orthogonal complement is the microscopic subspace. Thus functions in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} depend only on the coordinate y , whereas functions in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} have zero mean under \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} for \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y} -almost every y ."
    },
    {
      "id": "A2.SS1.p2",
      "coverage": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Block target/source conventions preserve future macro boundary.",
      "qualified_raw_slice": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p2-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
        "raw_bytes": 5889,
        "lf_bytes": 5889,
        "raw_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0",
        "lf_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0"
      },
      "qualified_LF_slice": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p2-dffe0a792ef0.LF.snapshot",
        "raw_bytes": 5889,
        "lf_bytes": 5889,
        "raw_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0",
        "lf_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0"
      },
      "byte_range": [
        727706,
        733595
      ],
      "literal_source_text": "Relative to the decomposition \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} , we write an operator \\mathsf{T} on \\mathfrak{H} in block form as \\mathsf{T}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\begin{aligned} \\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,,\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,.\\end{aligned} (B.3) The first subscript specifies the target subspace and the second the source subspace; thus \\mathsf{T}_{ab}:\\mathfrak{H}_{b}\\to\\mathfrak{H}_{a} for a,b\\in\\{\\mathsf{P},\\perp\\} ."
    },
    {
      "id": "A2.SS1.p3",
      "coverage": "NODE",
      "reason": "Selfadjoint unitary reflection gives scalar selfadjoint contraction context; printed B5 block conclusions separately EXCLUDED.",
      "qualified_raw_slice": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p3-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
        "raw_bytes": 8702,
        "lf_bytes": 8702,
        "raw_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873",
        "lf_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873"
      },
      "qualified_LF_slice": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p3-dffe0a792ef0.LF.snapshot",
        "raw_bytes": 8702,
        "lf_bytes": 8702,
        "raw_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873",
        "lf_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873"
      },
      "byte_range": [
        733596,
        742298
      ],
      "literal_source_text": "We first apply this block notation to the reflection map \\mathsf{U} from ( 2.14 ). We use the same symbol for its pullback on observables: (\\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq f(\\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\\,. (B.4) This pullback is self-adjoint and unitary, and hence has block matrix \\mathsf{U}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,. Here \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to itself, whereas \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} . Since \\mathsf{U} is self-adjoint and unitary, \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} is a self-adjoint contraction on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} . Writing \\mathsf{U}^{2}=I in blocks gives \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,. (B.5)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2.E8",
      "coverage": "NODE",
      "reason": "Yplus/Yminus reflection law context; no rate conclusion.",
      "qualified_raw_slice": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-E8-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
